description:
Core GenServer wrapping a ts_elixir Tailscale.Tcp.Stream handle.

State:
  - stream: Tailscale.Tcp.Stream.t() (opaque NIF resource)
  - owner: pid() (controlling process)
  - owner_mon: reference()
  - active: false | :once | true | integer()
  - mode: :binary | :list
  - buffer: binary() (for recv-with-length buffering)
  - packet: 0 (raw) — needed for SSL compat
  - header: 0 — needed for SSL compat
  - packet_size: 0 — needed for SSL compat
  - reader_task: reference() | nil (for active mode background reads)
  - remote_addr: {ip, port}
  - local_addr: {ip, port}
  - message_tags: {data_tag, closed_tag, error_tag, passive_tag} — configurable for SSL cb_info

Public API (gen_tcp-compatible):
  - send(socket, data) → :ok | {:error, reason}
  - recv(socket, length, timeout) → {:ok, data} | {:error, reason}
  - recv(socket, length) → recv(socket, length, :infinity)
  - controlling_process(socket, pid) → :ok | {:error, reason}
  - setopts(socket, opts) → :ok | {:error, reason}
  - getopts(socket, opts) → {:ok, opts} | {:error, reason}
  - close(socket) → :ok
  - shutdown(socket, how) → :ok | {:error, reason}
  - sockname(socket) → {:ok, {ip, port}} | {:error, reason}
  - peername(socket) → {:ok, {ip, port}} | {:error, reason}
  - port(socket) → {:ok, port} | {:error, reason}
  - getstat(socket) → {:ok, stats}
  - getstat(socket, opts) → {:ok, stats}

Active mode:
  When active != false, spawn a Task to call NIF recv.
  On data: send {data_tag, socket_ref, data} to owner.
  On :once, revert to false after one message.
  On true, re-arm immediately.
  On N, decrement and send {passive_tag, socket_ref} when reaching 0.

Recv buffering:
  If ts_elixir recv returns more than requested, store remainder in buffer.
  If ts_elixir recv returns less than requested (length > 0), accumulate until enough.
  If length == 0, return whatever is available.
